---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import AuthorityPanel from '@/components/ia/AuthorityPanel.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Programme"
  description="The Smart Property Data Trust Framework programme: its purpose, continuation, policy context and current direction."
>
  <PageMeta category="Programme" variant="brand" updated="Current programme view · 2026-08-18" />
  <h1>Programme</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The Smart Property Data Trust Framework (SPDTF) is an OPDA-led standards programme
    for trusted, connected property data. This page explains the continuation from the
    published PDTF 1.0 implementation into SPDTF 2.0 development.
  </p>

  <AuthorityPanel destination="programme" />

  <div class="callout callout--key">
    <p class="callout__label">The short version</p>
    <p>
      <strong>SPDTF 2.0 is in development, not adopted.</strong> PDTF 1.0 remains the
      published schema implementation and its derived corpus. Its individual ontology,
      model and mapping artefacts retain their own maturity; no replacement has been
      authorised by this programme view.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="continuation">A continuation, not a reset</h2>
  <p>
    PDTF 1.0 provides schemas, overlays, dictionaries, documentation and implementation
    evidence. SPDTF 2.0 development uses that material as attributed evidence alongside
    participant evidence, recognised sources and competency questions. Domain working
    groups then test meaning in bounded contexts before governance can promote any
    candidate.
  </p>
  <table>
    <caption>How the two bodies of work relate</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">PDTF 1.0</th><th scope="col">SPDTF 2.0 development</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Published schema implementation plus derived artefacts.</td><td>Evidence-up modelling and reviewable candidates.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Useful compatibility, constraint, coverage and migration evidence.</td><td>Human working groups own domain meaning; governance controls promotion.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Each child artefact keeps its own status.</td><td>Not a release, ratification or replacement standard.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="policy">UK Smart Data context</h2>
  <p>
    DBT Smart Data is external government policy and prospective scheme context. Property
    remains subject to feasibility, governance, legal assessment and consultation. OPDA
    contributes evidence and tested approaches; SPDTF is not an approved statutory
    property Smart Data scheme, and OPDA participation in government forums does not
    confer government authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    Read the official context in the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/smart-data-strategy" rel="noreferrer">Smart Data 2035 strategy</a>,
    the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/calls-for-evidence/smart-data-multi-sector-call-for-evidence" rel="noreferrer">multi-sector call for evidence</a>
    and the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/consultations/home-buying-and-selling-reform/outcome/home-buying-and-selling-reform-roadmap" rel="noreferrer">Home Buying and Selling Reform Roadmap</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="start">Choose a starting point</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2" title="SPDTF 2.0 Development" eyebrow="Develop" description="Follow the evidence-up method, ontologies journey, candidates and generated projections." />
    <GatewayCard href="/spdtf-2/working-groups" title="Working groups" eyebrow="Participate" description="Join the single SPDTF 2.0 working-group family, including Interoperability." />
    <GatewayCard href="/pdtf-1" title="PDTF 1.0" eyebrow="Implement" description="Find the published schema implementation and derived artefacts with their own status." />
    <GatewayCard href="/resources" title="Resources" eyebrow="Trace" description="Find attributed sources, programme records, standards references and historical material." />
  </div>
</Layout>
